  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2503.16416",
  "abstract": "The emergence of LLM-based agents has shifted the AI paradigm, enabling autonomous systems to plan, reason, and interact with dynamic environments. This survey provides a comprehensive overview of evaluation methodologies for these agents, focusing on four critical dimensions: fundamental agent capabilities, application-specific benchmarks, generalist agents, and evaluation frameworks.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "LLM-based agents integrate Large Language Models into a multi-step flow, maintaining a shared state and utilizing external tools to perform computations and interact with their environment. <strong>Evaluating these agents requires assessing their fundamental capabilities</strong>, including planning, tool use, self-reflection, and memory.",
